  "query_preview": "../ Thursday through Monday/... With an area of high \npressure in the Gulf of Alaska, a fairly benign weather pattern \nis expected to continue. Some shower activity is expected for \nwestern portions of the Panhandle. However, rainfall totals look \nfairly light with this activity. With the ridge of high pressure \nin the Gulf, expecting northwesterly winds of 5-10 kts in Clarence\nStrait, and perhaps up to 15 kts on the western side of Prince of\nWales Island. \n\nBy Saturday, the ridge of high pressure looks to move, and that\nwill lead to onshore flow, and some higher shower chances for the\nNorthern and Central Panhandle. Some showers moving in from\nBritish Columbia also appear possible, but confidence in this\noccurring is low due to model disagreements.",
